Subject: Route __openat64_nocancel through zsys_openat
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

__openat64_nocancel still made the openat syscall with inline asm, which
Fil-C refuses at run time ("cannot handle inline asm ... syscall"). Its
callers are nftw/ftw (on the first subdirectory), scandirat and glibc's
fts through __opendirat, so finit, libmount, libblkid, agetty and login
stopped the program. open64_nocancel and openat64 already call zsys_open
and zsys_openat the same way. The regression check is tests/glibc-dirwalk.nix.

--- a/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/openat64_nocancel.c	2026-11-04 20:47:43.645122122 +0100
+++ b/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/openat64_nocancel.c	2026-11-04 20:47:43.656497344 +0100
@@ -21,21 +21,12 @@
 
 #include <sysdep-cancel.h>
 #include <not-cancel.h>
+#include <pizlonated_syscalls.h>
 
 int
 __openat64_nocancel (int fd, const char *file, int oflag, ...)
 {
-  mode_t mode = 0;
-  if (__OPEN_NEEDS_MODE (oflag))
-    {
-      va_list arg;
-      va_start (arg, oflag);
-      mode = va_arg (arg, mode_t);
-      va_end (arg);
-    }
-
-  return INLINE_SYSCALL_CALL (openat, fd, file, oflag | O_LARGEFILE,
-			      mode);
+  return *(int *) zcall (zsys_openat, zargs ());
 }
 hidden_def (__openat64_nocancel)
 
